                        "tags": [
                            "singular",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "катафа́лке"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "f7927f78-e0fb-472b-8b0b-e27c089bb799",
                        "entry_id": "d02643b5-262b-3031-a49e-25890b1866c0",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "катафа́лках"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4d385642-09d1-34f5-8104-e55e3b964d75",
                        "entry_id": "d02643b5-262b-3031-a49e-25890b1866c0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "возвышение с траурными украшениями, на которое ставится гроб в помещении (при гражданской панихиде или в церкви при отпевании)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "14ae7ae8-18c4-48a1-b65b-ea42540a3bad",
                                "sense_id": "4d385642-09d1-34f5-8104-e55e3b964d75",
                                "text": "Гроб стоял на богатом катафалке под бархатным балдахином."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "eba30909-20e9-4b7d-a77a-2251d2ac6a0e",
                                "sense_id": "4d385642-09d1-34f5-8104-e55e3b964d75",
                                "text": "Он подошел к гробу, сел на ступеньки пышного катафалка, у самых ног покойницы, опустил голову на руку и призадумался."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "088429f7-d208-4af6-bcf2-02f7cc97b46e",
                                "sense_id": "4d385642-09d1-34f5-8104-e55e3b964d75",
                                "text": "Ещё мрачнее выглядела одна небольшая комната. В ней вместо кроватей стояли чёрные матовые столы и черные скамьи, походившие на половинки тех катафалков, которые приносятся гробовщиками в дом, где лежит покойник."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "37a27634-32b1-3d72-99dc-4265aedd1640",
                        "entry_id": "d02643b5-262b-3031-a49e-25890b1866c0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "транспортное средство, предназначенное для перевозки умерших"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c76341be-2f48-41ae-8fce-94c600619f98",
                                "sense_id": "37a27634-32b1-3d72-99dc-4265aedd1640",
                                "text": "Один за другим несли и везли на катафалках девятнадцать гробов, украшенных цветами."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a5a9fd01-77e5-313a-9388-0becde73af1b",
                        "entry_id": "d02643b5-262b-3031-a49e-25890b1866c0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен. неуклюжий, громоздкий автомобиль; автомобиль в плохом техническом состоянии"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5b328426-0760-4d97-8a1e-57e4487dd06c",
                                "sense_id": "a5a9fd01-77e5-313a-9388-0becde73af1b",
                                "text": "Убери свой катафалк от подъезда!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9939a2ff-7341-4d32-a5d7-6b85632d8bdc",
                        "source_entry_id": "d02643b5-262b-3031-a49e-25890b1866c0",
                        "source_sense_description": "возвышение",
                        "target_lang_word": "catafalque",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "catafalque",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e650ae62-47b6-388a-9015-dbc18765189e",
                                        "entry_id": "4fcb59b4-b2c2-34fb-9f93-d1e009808261",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A platform used to display or convey a coffin during a funeral, often ornate."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f05e077-82f1-4fb4-a785-a996a9cd5a94",
                                                "sense_id": "e650ae62-47b6-388a-9015-dbc18765189e",
                                                "text": "Until noon, the hour of the funeral, crowds continued to file by the plain pine coffin on its plain flower-covered catafalque."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "978f0ecb-e775-42eb-8cd7-8bbf5dc0f813",
                                                "sense_id": "e650ae62-47b6-388a-9015-dbc18765189e",
                                                "text": "After another brief funeral rite at Tzu Hu, the presidential casket was laid on the catafalque in the central hall of a temporary “mausoleum” and sealed with marble slabs. There, the body of President Chiang will rest pending permanent burial in the mainland after its recovery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58e68465-24a2-425a-afec-cf4d78f37c91",
                                                "sense_id": "e650ae62-47b6-388a-9015-dbc18765189e",
                                                "text": "The period of official mourning was long-drawn-out even by the standards of the day; the funeral ceremony held in Avignon's cathedral lasted a full nine days, with the pope's catafalque hung with black silk beneath candelabra likewise draped in black."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b06cf12d-1dbd-45b9-ae69-db2de4dfb3f9",
                        "source_entry_id": "d02643b5-262b-3031-a49e-25890b1866c0",
                        "source_sense_description": "возвышение",
                        "target_lang_word": "bier",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bier",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6fd10d49-9112-3725-b980-a0fd861d77b8",
                                        "entry_id": "e15bd6dc-0540-33cd-892a-4b74c2068b31",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A litter to transport the corpse of a dead person."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c0c9b2b4-0288-4f40-98ef-85d69bde763a",
                                                "sense_id": "6fd10d49-9112-3725-b980-a0fd861d77b8",
                                                "text": "They bore him bare-faced on the bier."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "befb515a-37f4-3aa3-88db-4f411917a9a0",
                                        "entry_id": "e15bd6dc-0540-33cd-892a-4b74c2068b31",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A platform or stand where a body or coffin is placed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2fe33376-267d-4d39-87bf-ce1d1749d9c1",
                                                "sense_id": "befb515a-37f4-3aa3-88db-4f411917a9a0",
                                                "text": "On April 5, 1925, Chiang Kai-shek returned from the First Eastern Expedition to the Whampoa Military Academy to officiate at a funeral service for Sun Yat-sen, who had died in Peking on March 12. Huang Chi-lu, then a young professor of political science at the University of Kwangtung and destined to become director of the Kuomintang Archives some forty years later, has informed us of the display of strong emotion evidenced by Chiang on this occasion: \"The service was officiated by Mr. Chiang and Liao Chung-k'ai and was attended by over four thousand officers, cadets, and soldiers. As the funeral ceremonies began, Mr. Chiang, unable to control himself, wept bitterly and audibly, causing all in the assembly to shed tears.\"¹ Three years later, at the conclusion of the Northern Expedition, a similarly melodramatic scene unfolded before the eyes of the public as Chiang visited Sun's bier in the suburbs of Peking."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28f78f0e-09d3-3a3e-84da-ab26d16a8f54",
                                        "entry_id": "e15bd6dc-0540-33cd-892a-4b74c2068b31",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A count of forty threads in the warp or chain of woollen cloth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a88f57fa-9f9f-4959-8657-92e516c8c7da",
                        "source_entry_id": "d02643b5-262b-3031-a49e-25890b1866c0",
                        "source_sense_description": "транспортное средство",
                        "target_lang_word": "hearse",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hearse",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "16623f29-4791-31f3-9161-0734083c52b4",
                                        "entry_id": "9811c9da-e281-31b3-ae34-b208af43dc79",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A framework of wood or metal placed over the coffin or tomb of a deceased person, and covered with a pall; also, a temporary canopy bearing wax lights and set up in a church, under which the coffin was placed during the funeral ceremonies."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c3e980ad-50b5-3ec5-b964-f2915b794aca",
                                        "entry_id": "9811c9da-e281-31b3-ae34-b208af43dc79",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A grave, coffin, tomb, or sepulchral monument."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b69930a-5df8-41fb-8c13-72611af0b946",
                                                "sense_id": "c3e980ad-50b5-3ec5-b964-f2915b794aca",
                                                "text": "underneath this sable hearse"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3a8cf5cb-3562-4ccc-b06e-b422e16b1e9f",
                                                "sense_id": "c3e980ad-50b5-3ec5-b964-f2915b794aca",
                                                "text": "Beside the hearse a fruitful palm tree grows,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "610b56c4-ae67-486a-8d7e-fe25425c9fd4",
                                                "sense_id": "c3e980ad-50b5-3ec5-b964-f2915b794aca",
                                                "text": "who lies beneath this sculptured hearse"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f01544ff-0706-30ab-aecc-c718b09ee16d",
                                        "entry_id": "9811c9da-e281-31b3-ae34-b208af43dc79",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A bier or handbarrow for conveying the dead to the grave."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7da8d72-e4b3-4ac0-b71e-2bd88a5b5fd1",
                                                "sense_id": "f01544ff-0706-30ab-aecc-c718b09ee16d",
                                                "text": "Set down, set down your honourable load, / If honour may be shrouded in a hearse."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "cf97d36a-2b5d-3762-bff1-60cc8158b3bc",
                                        "entry_id": "9811c9da-e281-31b3-ae34-b208af43dc79",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A carriage or vehicle specially adapted or used for transporting a dead person to the place of funeral or to the grave."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "hearse",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ee807e6-dcb1-353c-b68d-4b488a5bea72",
                                        "entry_id": "3ee2368a-699b-3422-8e7a-bdd9db651582",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To enclose in a hearse; to entomb."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "dated"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
